<h2 class="bold" id="progressive-enhancement-of-a-select-element"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="autocomplete#progressive-enhancement-of-a-select-element">Progressive enhancement of a select element</a></h2>
<p>If your autocomplete is meant to select from a small list of options (a few hundred), we strongly suggest that you render a <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token code-tag punctuation" style="color:hsl(119, 34%, 47%)">&lt;</span><span class="token code-tag" style="color:hsl(5, 74%, 59%)">select</span><span class="token code-tag punctuation" style="color:hsl(119, 34%, 47%)">&gt;</span></span></code></span> on the server, and use <a href="https://github.com/alphagov/accessible-autocomplete#progressive-enhancement" class="underline">progressive enhancement</a>.</p>
<p>ODS Autocomplete wrapper javascript automatically uses progressive enhancement when initalized on a select element.</p>
